          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#functoriality Functoriality
          #FunctorialityOfLinearPermutationRepresentations.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (functoriality of linear permutation representations)
            %p
              The construction of linear permutation representations (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LinearPermutationRepresentation"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+G-sets"} category of G-sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Set
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+representations"} category of linear representations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mi Rep
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Rep
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mi Set
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                    %mi G
                    %mi Rep
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G Set
                    \\overset{ \phantom{AA} k[-] \phantom{AA} }{\longrightarrow}
                    G Rep
                    \\,.
            %p
              Both of these categories are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig+categories"} rig categories
              with respect to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              on the left, and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+representations"} tensor product of representations
              on the right.
            %p
              The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k[-]
              is canonically a homomorphism of rig-categories in that in that it is canonically a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal functor
              for both “addition” and “multiplication”
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal structures
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
